Voice ID (0.8.10; fetched when you set it up, not included in the package):
- CAM++ speaker verification models from 3D-Speaker (Alibaba DAMO Academy, https://github.com/modelscope/3D-Speaker),
  Apache License 2.0: speech_campplus_sv_en_voxceleb_16k (trained on VoxCeleb2, whose annotations are CC BY 4.0) and
  speech_campplus_sv_zh_en_16k-common_advanced (https://www.modelscope.cn/models/iic/), in the ONNX conversions by
  k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), Apache License 2.0.
- kaldi-native-fbank (https://github.com/csukuangfj/kaldi-native-fbank), Apache License 2.0; onnxruntime, MIT; numpy,
  BSD-3-Clause.
The impostor sets in src/kurooto/data/voiceid/ (when present) are speaker embeddings computed with those models from
LibriSpeech's dev and test sets (Panayotov, Chen, Povey and Khudanpur, 2015; https://www.openslr.org/12), licensed
CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changed: only computed vectors are kept, no audio, speaker
ids or transcripts. The *-phone sets (0.9.2) are computed the same way after passing the audio through a simulated
phone channel (equalising, gain, band-limiting, mu-law, a short room tail and noise).
